    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2x^3+5x^2-x-6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+2)(2x+3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=2x^3+5x^2-x-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=2+5-1-6\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x-1$ is a factor. In long division, the successive quotient terms are $2x^2$, $7x$ and $6$:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)-2x^2(x-1)&=7x^2-x-6\\\\(7x^2-x-6)-7x(x-1)&=6x-6\\\\(6x-6)-6(x-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(2x^2+7x+6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(2x+3)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2x^3+x^2-7x-6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-2)(x+1)(2x+3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=2x^3+x^2-7x-6$. Testing integer factors of the constant term:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=2+1-7-6=-10\\\\P(-1)&=-2+1+7-6=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x+1$ is a factor. In long division, the successive quotient terms are $2x^2$, $-x$ and $-6$:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)-2x^2(x+1)&=-x^2-7x-6\\\\(-x^2-7x-6)-(-x)(x+1)&=-6x-6\\\\(-6x-6)-(-6)(x+1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(2x^2-x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(2x+3)(x-2).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 90
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2x^4-x^3-8x^2+x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-2)(x-1)(x+1)(2x+3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=2x^4-x^3-8x^2+x+6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=2-1-8+1+6\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x-1$ is a factor. Long division gives:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)-2x^3(x-1)&=x^3-8x^2+x+6\\\\(x^3-8x^2+x+6)-x^2(x-1)&=-7x^2+x+6\\\\(-7x^2+x+6)-(-7x)(x-1)&=-6x+6\\\\(-6x+6)-(-6)(x-1)&=0\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(2x^3+x^2-7x-6).\\end{align*}$$\nLet $Q(x)=2x^3+x^2-7x-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(-1)&=-2+1+7-6\\\\Q(-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nDivide $Q(x)$ by $x+1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(x)-2x^2(x+1)&=-x^2-7x-6\\\\(-x^2-7x-6)-(-x)(x+1)&=-6x-6\\\\(-6x-6)-(-6)(x+1)&=0\\\\Q(x)&=(x+1)(2x^2-x-6)\\\\Q(x)&=(x+1)(2x+3)(x-2).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $P(x)=(x-1)(x+1)(2x+3)(x-2)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 125
      }
    ]
